					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5295</guid>
				<title>SCP-5295</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5295</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item #:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5295&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object Class:&lt;/strong&gt; Euclid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; Access to SCP-5295 is restricted to regularly scheduled maintenance and feedings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cleaning and maintenance routines should be as with non-anomalous site facilities. In the event of malfunction, repair of SCP-5295 should be prioritised.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Feeding is to be carried out by supervised D-class personnel twice weekly, with approximately 5kg of meat (species irrelevant). D-class should place the food next to SCP-5295, activate, then exit the chamber promptly. If D-class has for any reason not exited the chamber within 20 seconds, the door should be locked and the next feeding may be skipped.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5295 is to be connected only to a small, isolated plumbing system, including septic tank. When the tank requires emptying, this should be done by D-class personnel no less than two days after a feeding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Under no circumstances is any person to urinate, defecate or vomit into SCP-5295.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5295 is a faded white porcelain flush toilet estimated to date from the mid-1980s. A mostly faded stamp on the side of the cistern indicates the manufacturer to be █████. In appearance and physical composition it is unremarkable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When SCP-5295 is used in the conventional fashion, a Type-C event may occur. Type-C events do not always occur on use, with the likelihood of an event primarily being linked to the sex of the user&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-720671-1&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; and the length of time since last feeding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Type-C events are marked by the manifestation of the entity SCP-5295-1, an aggressive, carnivorous humanoid. Manifestation occurs within the plumbing attached to SCP-5295, generally at a distance of 5-10m from the U-bend. In a typical event, SCP-5295-1 will exit the bowl, attack the legs of its target with teeth and claws to prevent escape, then return into SCP-5295 and the attached plumbing, bringing the target with it&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-720671-2&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discovery:&lt;/strong&gt; The Foundation was alerted to a potential anomaly by an agent embedded in law enforcement in the city of ████████, England, after a malformed human skull was discovered in a local sewage treatment plant. It was identified as belonging to Jim Hooker&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-720671-3&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;, a man from a nearby village who had recently been reported missing. Foundation agents interviewed Hooker&#039;s wife, Amanda Hooker, at their home and were able to identify SCP-5295 as anomalous. It was removed and replaced with a non-anomalous model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;Interview&amp;nbsp;Log&amp;nbsp;5295-01-AH&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;Interview&amp;nbsp;Log&amp;nbsp;5295-01-AH&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interviewed:&lt;/strong&gt; Amanda Hooker, wife of James Hooker, suspected deceased via anomalous means.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interviewers:&lt;/strong&gt; Agents Wren and Cooke&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Foreword:&lt;/strong&gt; Agents visited in the guise of local law enforcement to ascertain if Mrs. Hooker had any useful information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;lt;Begin Audio Log, 13:41&amp;gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooke:&lt;/strong&gt; -aying nobody ever really spoke to them. Kinda rough sorts, y&#039;know? Recording now, by the way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wren:&lt;/strong&gt; Mmhmm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooke:&lt;/strong&gt; The place looks normal enough from out here, right? Bit of a shithole, but nothing that&#039;s our kind of weird.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wren:&lt;/strong&gt; Hmmm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooke:&lt;/strong&gt; Well fuck me, don&#039;t get too into it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;[A few seconds of silence, then the sound of a door opening.]&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wren:&lt;/strong&gt; Mrs. Hooker?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AH:&lt;/strong&gt; Is&amp;#8230;is it about Jim?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;[A brief pause and the sound of a person sniffing.]&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooke:&lt;/strong&gt; Can we come inside for a few minutes?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AH:&lt;/strong&gt;Sure, um, yeah, come in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;[Footsteps, then the sound of something being picked up.]]&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooke:&lt;/strong&gt; This you and Jim here?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AH:&lt;/strong&gt; Wha- oh, yes. That was, um, just after the honeymoon. We went to Skegness&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-720671-4&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;. Couldn&#039;t go abroad because, uh, my condition, y&#039;know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooke:&lt;/strong&gt; Right, course. And how old are they now? Are they around?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AH:&lt;/strong&gt; No, h-he&amp;#8230;he&#039;s, um, you know. Gone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooke:&lt;/strong&gt; Ah. I&#039;m sorry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;[More footsteps, then the creaking of chairs being sat on. There is a pause, then a throat being cleared.]&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wren:&lt;/strong&gt; Mrs. Hooker, I&#039;m sorry but there isn&#039;t really an easy way to say this. Yesterday evening, we recovered your husband&#039;s remains just outside ████████.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AH:&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;#8230;remains?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wren:&lt;/strong&gt; Yes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AH:&lt;/strong&gt; Oh.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;[Silence.]&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AH:&lt;/strong&gt; D-did he&amp;#8230;I mean, do you know&amp;#8230;how?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooke&lt;/strong&gt;: Well, we&#039;re looking into that, and hopefully you can help us a little. Can you tell us anything about the day he disappeared? The report I&#039;ve seen says you were at your mother&#039;s, right?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AH:&lt;/strong&gt; We&#039;d had, um, an argument. B-but not like - I mean - I wouldn&#039;t have-&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wren:&lt;/strong&gt; You&#039;re not under suspicion, Mrs. Hooker. We just want to know if there was anything that might have been&amp;#8230;out of the ordinary. A sudden change in behaviour, noises you can&#039;t quite explain, maybe even seeing things that aren&#039;t really there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AH:&lt;/strong&gt;Like&amp;#8230;ghosts?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wren:&lt;/strong&gt; Sure. Like ghosts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;[A brief pause.]&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AH:&lt;/strong&gt; Um&amp;#8230;where did you say you found him?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooke:&lt;/strong&gt; The remains we found had washed up at a local water treatment plant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;[There is a pause, an inaudible murmur&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-720671-5&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;, then a thump.]&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooke:&lt;/strong&gt; Fuck, Mrs Hooker?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;[Sounds of movement]&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wren:&lt;/strong&gt; She&#039;s breathing. I think she&#039;s just fainted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooke:&lt;/strong&gt; I didn&#039;t think people actually did that. Shit, should we, like, do something?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wren:&lt;/strong&gt; She&#039;ll probably come round in a minute, just get her a glass of water.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooke:&lt;/strong&gt; Sure, sure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;[Footsteps, a tap running, then the sound of banging cupboard doors]&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wren:&lt;/strong&gt; Jesus, Dave, it&#039;s only a glass of water.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooke:&lt;/strong&gt; I&#039;m just having a poke round.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;[More banging.]&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooke:&lt;/strong&gt; Fridge is kinda weird.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wren:&lt;/strong&gt; Specifically??&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooke:&lt;/strong&gt; We&#039;ve got&amp;#8230;six whole chickens in here. Dates handwritten on them. Every three days, it looks like.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wren:&lt;/strong&gt; What&#039;s the first one?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooke:&lt;/strong&gt; ██/██/████&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-720671-6&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wren:&lt;/strong&gt; Well shit. Let&#039;s take her back to site, we&#039;ve definitely got something going on here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooke:&lt;/strong&gt; Yeah, for sure. Give me a minute though.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wren:&lt;/strong&gt; What&#039;s up?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cooke:&lt;/strong&gt; It&#039;s like an hour drive back, I&#039;m going for a piss first.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;[A sigh]&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wren:&lt;/strong&gt; Just make it quick.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;[Agent Cooke pauses recording. It is not resumed]&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;lt;End Log, 13:50&amp;gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Closing Statement:&lt;/strong&gt; Mrs. Hooker was remanded in Foundation custody for further questioning but upon rousing became withdrawn and uncooperative. She was placed into a standard humanoid containment cell overnight while SCP-5295&#039;s removal was carried out. The next morning, Mrs. Hooker was discovered to have drowned herself in the bowl of the toilet in her cell. Agent Cooke&#039;s remains were quietly retrieved from ███████ sewage treatment works two days later.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rebel-diamond&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1345140&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1608281518&quot; alt=&quot;Rebel_Diamond&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1345140)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rebel-diamond&quot;  &gt;Rebel_Diamond&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnotes-footer&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Footnotes&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-720671-1&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;. Male users are approximately four times more likely to initiate a Type-C event.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-720671-2&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;2&lt;/a&gt;. Recovered remains display rapid-onset acute osteomalacia. It is believed this is deliberately inflicted by SCP-5295-1 to enable transport of victims through SCP-5295 without damage.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-720671-3&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;3&lt;/a&gt;. Hooker&#039;s DNA having been sampled by law enforcement some years earlier after an arrest for Assault occasioning Actual Bodily Harm&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-720671-4&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;4&lt;/a&gt;. A once-popular tourist town on the East coast of England.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-720671-5&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;5&lt;/a&gt;. Agent Wren later reported that he believed Mrs. Hooker had mumbled to herself &amp;quot;Like a fucking goldfish, Jim&amp;quot;, though could offer no explanation for these words.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;footnote-footer&quot; id=&quot;footnote-720671-6&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;  &gt;6&lt;/a&gt;. The date of Mr Hooker&#039;s reported disappearance.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</description>
