						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p><strong>Item #:</strong> SCP-5295</p> <p><strong>Object Class:</strong> Euclid</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> Access to SCP-5295 is restricted to regularly scheduled maintenance and feedings.</p> <p>Cleaning and maintenance routines should be as with non-anomalous site facilities. In the event of malfunction, repair of SCP-5295 should be prioritised.</p> <p>Feeding is to be carried out by supervised D-class personnel twice weekly, with approximately 5kg of meat (species irrelevant). D-class should place the food next to SCP-5295, activate, then exit the chamber promptly. If D-class has for any reason not exited the chamber within 20 seconds, the door should be locked and the next feeding may be skipped.</p> <p>SCP-5295 is to be connected only to a small, isolated plumbing system, including septic tank. When the tank requires emptying, this should be done by D-class personnel no less than two days after a feeding.</p> <p>Under no circumstances is any person to urinate, defecate or vomit into SCP-5295.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5295 is a faded white porcelain flush toilet estimated to date from the mid-1980s. A mostly faded stamp on the side of the cistern indicates the manufacturer to be █████. In appearance and physical composition it is unremarkable.</p> <p>When SCP-5295 is used in the conventional fashion, a Type-C event may occur. Type-C events do not always occur on use, with the likelihood of an event primarily being linked to the sex of the user<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-598205-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup> and the length of time since last feeding.</p> <p>Type-C events are marked by the manifestation of the entity SCP-5295-1, an aggressive, carnivorous humanoid. Manifestation occurs within the plumbing attached to SCP-5295, generally at a distance of 5-10m from the U-bend. In a typical event, SCP-5295-1 will exit the bowl, attack the legs of its target with teeth and claws to prevent escape, then return into SCP-5295 and the attached plumbing, bringing the target with it<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-598205-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >2</a></sup>.</p> <p><strong>Discovery:</strong> The Foundation was alerted to a potential anomaly by an agent embedded in law enforcement in the city of ████████, England, after a malformed human skull was discovered in a local sewage treatment plant. It was identified as belonging to Jim Hooker<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-598205-3" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >3</a></sup>, a man from a nearby village who had recently been reported missing. Foundation agents interviewed Hooker's wife, Amanda Hooker, at their home and were able to identify SCP-5295 as anomalous. It was removed and replaced with a non-anomalous model.</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Interview&nbsp;Log&nbsp;5295-01-AH</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Interview&nbsp;Log&nbsp;5295-01-AH</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <blockquote> <p><strong>Interviewed:</strong> Amanda Hooker, wife of James Hooker, suspected deceased via anomalous means.</p> <p><strong>Interviewers:</strong> Agents Wren and Cooke</p> <p><strong>Foreword:</strong> Agents visited in the guise of local law enforcement to ascertain if Mrs. Hooker had any useful information.</p> <p><strong>&lt;Begin Audio Log, 13:41&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>Cooke:</strong> -aying nobody ever really spoke to them. Kinda rough sorts, y'know? Recording now, by the way.</p> <p><strong>Wren:</strong> Mmhmm.</p> <p><strong>Cooke:</strong> The place looks normal enough from out here, right? Bit of a shithole, but nothing that's our kind of weird.</p> <p><strong>Wren:</strong> Hmmm.</p> <p><strong>Cooke:</strong> Well fuck me, don't get too into it.</p> <p><em>[A few seconds of silence, then the sound of a door opening.]</em></p> <p><strong>Wren:</strong> Mrs. Hooker?</p> <p><strong>AH:</strong> Is&#8230;is it about Jim?</p> <p><em>[A brief pause and the sound of a person sniffing.]</em></p> <p><strong>Cooke:</strong> Can we come inside for a few minutes?</p> <p><strong>AH:</strong>Sure, um, yeah, come in.</p> <p><em>[Footsteps, then the sound of something being picked up.]]</em></p> <p><strong>Cooke:</strong> This you and Jim here?</p> <p><strong>AH:</strong> Wha- oh, yes. That was, um, just after the honeymoon. We went to Skegness<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-598205-4" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >4</a></sup>. Couldn't go abroad because, uh, my condition, y'know.</p> <p><strong>Cooke:</strong> Right, course. And how old are they now? Are they around?</p> <p><strong>AH:</strong> No, h-he&#8230;he's, um, you know. Gone.</p> <p><strong>Cooke:</strong> Ah. I'm sorry.</p> <p><em>[More footsteps, then the creaking of chairs being sat on. There is a pause, then a throat being cleared.]</em></p> <p><strong>Wren:</strong> Mrs. Hooker, I'm sorry but there isn't really an easy way to say this. Yesterday evening, we recovered your husband's remains just outside ████████.</p> <p><strong>AH:</strong> &#8230;remains?</p> <p><strong>Wren:</strong> Yes.</p> <p><strong>AH:</strong> Oh.</p> <p><em>[Silence.]</em></p> <p><strong>AH:</strong> D-did he&#8230;I mean, do you know&#8230;how?</p> <p><strong>Cooke</strong>: Well, we're looking into that, and hopefully you can help us a little. Can you tell us anything about the day he disappeared? The report I've seen says you were at your mother's, right?</p> <p><strong>AH:</strong> We'd had, um, an argument. B-but not like - I mean - I wouldn't have-</p> <p><strong>Wren:</strong> You're not under suspicion, Mrs. Hooker. We just want to know if there was anything that might have been&#8230;out of the ordinary. A sudden change in behaviour, noises you can't quite explain, maybe even seeing things that aren't really there.</p> <p><strong>AH:</strong>Like&#8230;ghosts?</p> <p><strong>Wren:</strong> Sure. Like ghosts.</p> <p><em>[A brief pause.]</em></p> <p><strong>AH:</strong> Um&#8230;where did you say you found him?</p> <p><strong>Cooke:</strong> The remains we found had washed up at a local water treatment plant.</p> <p><em>[There is a pause, an inaudible murmur<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-598205-5" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >5</a></sup>, then a thump.]</em></p> <p><strong>Cooke:</strong> Fuck, Mrs Hooker?</p> <p><em>[Sounds of movement]</em></p> <p><strong>Wren:</strong> She's breathing. I think she's just fainted.</p> <p><strong>Cooke:</strong> I didn't think people actually did that. Shit, should we, like, do something?</p> <p><strong>Wren:</strong> She'll probably come round in a minute, just get her a glass of water.</p> <p><strong>Cooke:</strong> Sure, sure.</p> <p><em>[Footsteps, a tap running, then the sound of banging cupboard doors]</em></p> <p><strong>Wren:</strong> Jesus, Dave, it's only a glass of water.</p> <p><strong>Cooke:</strong> I'm just having a poke round.</p> <p><em>[More banging.]</em></p> <p><strong>Cooke:</strong> Fridge is kinda weird.</p> <p><strong>Wren:</strong> Specifically??</p> <p><strong>Cooke:</strong> We've got&#8230;six whole chickens in here. Dates handwritten on them. Every three days, it looks like.</p> <p><strong>Wren:</strong> What's the first one?</p> <p><strong>Cooke:</strong> ██/██/████<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-598205-6" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >6</a></sup></p> <p><strong>Wren:</strong> Well shit. Let's take her back to site, we've definitely got something going on here.</p> <p><strong>Cooke:</strong> Yeah, for sure. Give me a minute though.</p> <p><strong>Wren:</strong> What's up?</p> <p><strong>Cooke:</strong> It's like an hour drive back, I'm going for a piss first.</p> <p><em>[A sigh]</em></p> <p><strong>Wren:</strong> Just make it quick.</p> <p><em>[Agent Cooke pauses recording. It is not resumed]</em></p> <p><strong>&lt;End Log, 13:50&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>Closing Statement:</strong> Mrs. Hooker was remanded in Foundation custody for further questioning but upon rousing became withdrawn and uncooperative. She was placed into a standard humanoid containment cell overnight while SCP-5295's removal was carried out. The next morning, Mrs. Hooker was discovered to have drowned herself in the bowl of the toilet in her cell. Agent Cooke's remains were quietly retrieved from ███████ sewage treatment works two days later.</p> </blockquote> </div> </div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rebel-diamond" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1345140&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608281518" alt="Rebel_Diamond" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1345140)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rebel-diamond" >Rebel_Diamond</a></span></p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-598205-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. Male users are approximately four times more likely to initiate a Type-C event.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-598205-2"><a href="javascript:;" >2</a>. Recovered remains display rapid-onset acute osteomalacia. It is believed this is deliberately inflicted by SCP-5295-1 to enable transport of victims through SCP-5295 without damage.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-598205-3"><a href="javascript:;" >3</a>. Hooker's DNA having been sampled by law enforcement some years earlier after an arrest for Assault occasioning Actual Bodily Harm</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-598205-4"><a href="javascript:;" >4</a>. A once-popular tourist town on the East coast of England.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-598205-5"><a href="javascript:;" >5</a>. Agent Wren later reported that he believed Mrs. Hooker had mumbled to herself &quot;Like a fucking goldfish, Jim&quot;, though could offer no explanation for these words.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-598205-6"><a href="javascript:;" >6</a>. The date of Mr Hooker's reported disappearance.</div> </div> 
